ve to look at  the young quarterbacks and who's doing  well I'm here in Tampa so I hear all the  excitement about the blocks and you see  what Jameis Winston is doing and the  confidence they have in him Weston  Mariota was a one two picks a couple of  years back and I think they're about  ready to take off the teams have gotten  better on the  since they get the box have put a ton of  skill position players around Jameis I  look for those through teams to be very  good this year yeah I think and yeah I  agree with you on both of them I think  both teams take that next step I think  Tampa should play up team you know the  one thing that worries being about  Winston is he might be too confident  well that's what they're working on I  know from talking to the coaches and  saying things down here you don't have  to make every single play every play  doesn't have to be a touchdown you don't  have to be the focal point and now the  more people they're getting around him  I think that'll help we went through  that with Peyton when I got there to  Indianapolis our defense wasn't quite  ready yet he was used to having to take  chances having to win games  31:28 so you feel like I've got to do it  on every plate I think Jameis will learn  that and relax and say you know what  it's not going to be the worst thing to  punt it's not going to be the worst  thing to throw this ball away and go to  second down and that's going to help  them when that message gets through to  him any other teams that you're looking  at whether they're going to be better  than what you think or maybe worse than  what you think  well you know I saw the Cowboys at the  Hall of Fame game and that is an  interesting team to me because I think  they have a lot of things in place to I  got to spend some time with dak Prescott  and he was super impressive as a young  quarterback too but this Elliott  situation I think that has everything  kind of in limbo there and what's going  to happen how will they be 