sive lineman who said the same  thing I'm going to you know have a  protest all year and there hasn't been  hardly anything said about that so I did  I thought that was an ideal place for  him to go I also saw the story where you  challenged  Tampa's professional sports teams to  help pay to move a Confederate statue  from front and in front of the local  courthouse there and explain how that  came up and what was the response from  those teams in the tamp area play was a  great response it was an odd situation  they've been talking about this statute  for a month and the County Commission  has gone back and forth they said  they're going to move it everyone  thought it was a done deal that it was  moved and then in yesterday's paper  there was an article that said everyone  thinks is a good eye  they voted 42 to move it but they don't  have the funds and they're not going to  move it unless private funds come  available and they wanted 140,000  dollars in 30 days in the article they  said we don't know if we're going to get  this done and to me it just seems a  little bit ridiculous so my wife and I  decided that we would help out and do  something that we could do we  contributed and then I said you know on  social media we need to get people  behind this and I'm going to start with  the this fourth thing and the response  was unbelievable and not only from the  blocks and the Rays and the lightning  which was gratifying but just from  people giving $5 $10 and so in about six  hours that they raised the money  $140,000 and they had to stop taking  payment so it was gratifying to see the  citizens get behind what everybody  thought was the right thing to do I  won't say everybody but most people what  do you see when you see those statues  well I think as an African American you  see the legacy of slavery and people  fighting to keep slavery in existence  and it may not be offensive to everybody  but it's offensive to a significant part  of our community and we didn't think it  should be on government property in a  government place and that was design I  think everyone agreed with it but then  the question was how to do it and what  to do it and I think a lot of people  just validated everyone's concerned and  said this is something that we should  move not on government property not  honoring a legacy that was offensive to  so many people so you don't have a  problem if it's somewhere else you just  don't think it should be on government  property that was my opinion if where is  it going to be relocated I'm not exactly  sure it's a private family that's  begging it a private Cemetery or  something I'm not totally sure but it's  not a it's not a government property  where it's going to you grew up in  Detroit do what do you remember about  the Detroit riots I just saw the movie  yesterday with my wife and it brought  back some memories I was 11 years old  didn't really understand everything that  was going on  my uncle ended up going into the police  department right after that and rise  into you know Assistant Chief of Police  in Detroit you know just feeling like  there needed to be some overhauls in the  way we did things but I remember you  know dr. King getting killed the whole  thing and it just discontent didn't know  what it was all about didn't understand  it of course I had to talk to my dad  some to learn about segregation and you  know he spent time in Washington DC and  went through segregation so it was all  new to me as a young young kid but there  was frustration and discontent that's  what I remember  eleven-year-old pretty powerful movie  very very great shock you tone I'll see  you in New England or the Patriots going  undefeated this year I don't know if  they'll go undefeated but they got a  pretty solid seed number stuff that but  it's damn and then everybody else  there's nobody on their level this year  no you know that's how it always starts  out that way everybody thinks the  defending champions are on beat and if I  was a betting man I wouldn't bet on the  paper it's not because I don't think  that the best team I just think it's  hard to repeat it's not done that often  so if you have the Patriots versus the  field I would take the field and say  there's somebody that's going to come  out of nowhere and then rise up are we  going to have an awkward situation again  where Bill Belichick walks by and he  greets you and then he greets Rodney and  then he gets to me and then he just  keeps going like remember was at the  Meadowlands when they had the button  back that I think that could happen kind  of awkward yeah I know it's like a coach  Rodney I don't know what you did to kind  of do anything I didn't do anything  Thank You tone I'll see in a few days  looking forward to it all right that's  Tony Dungy Continental Tire coaches  corner Continental Tire the official  tire Major League Soccer soccer fans  expect peak performance on the pitch and  also demand peak performance on the  street that's why Continental was built  a tire for what you do whether you're  heading to the game taking the kids to  practice Continental was engineered a  line of tires that includes the  best-in-class wet braking superb  handling Continental Tire proud  supporter of the Dan Patrick show visit  Continental Tire calm to learn more the  Dan Patrick show weekday mornings on  audience

